  "rulings": {
    "references": [
      {
        "link": "https://world.digimoncard.com/rule/?card_no=BT17-084#qaResult_card",
        "num": 1,
        "text": "Official English Q&A for BT17-084 (Sep. 6, 2024)"
      }
    ],
    "rulings": [
      {
        "answer": "Yes, you can.  Even if the part after the conditions specified with \"by X\" in an effect can't be resolved, the effect can still activate.",
        "question": "Can I use this card's [All Turns] effect to suspend this Tamer when my level 5 or higher [Free] trait Digimon would be deleted in battle, even if I don't have any level 4 or lower Digimon cards in that Digimon's digivolution cards?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "No, you can't.  The card is removed from digivolution cards before ＜Retaliation＞ can activate.",
        "question": "When my level 5 or higher [Free] trait Digimon would be deleted in battle, I used this card's [All Turns] effect to play a level 4 or lower Digimon card with ＜Retaliation＞ in its inherited effects from that Digimon's digivolution cards. Can I use ＜Retaliation＞ to delete the battled opponent's Digimon at such times?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "No, you can't.  This card's [End of Your Turn] effect does not allow you to attack with Digimon that are in a state where they can't attack.",
        "question": "Can I use this card's [End of Your Turn] effect to attack even when the [Free] trait Digimon is suspended?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "No, you can't.  The effect will trigger on both copies, but after the attack declaration is made for the 1st Digimon and effects such as [When Attacking] effects have finished activating, the effect on the 2nd copy of this card that was pending activation will activate before the counter timing. However, a new attack declaration can't be made during an attack, and only the 1st Digimon's attack can be performed as a result.",
        "question": "When I have 2 copies of this Tamer and 2 unsuspended [Free] trait Digimon, can I activate the [End of Your Turn] effect on both copies of this card and attack using both of the [Free] trait Digimon?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      }
    ]
  },
